<title>UK: Details of 4.12 pct UK 1996 car registrations gain.</title>
<headline>Details of 4.12 pct UK 1996 car registrations gain.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's SMMT Ltd auto trade body issued the following details of new car registrations for December, 1996 showing how registrations rose by what it called a &quot;healthy&quot; 9.23 percent in the month to give a 4.12 percent rise for whole of the calendar year.</p>
<p>December</p>
<p>Top 10 by marque, market share in pct vs year ago.  Ford	  14,887  (19.05 pct) vs  10,912  (15.31 pct)</p>
<p> Rover	 13,205  (16.90 pct) vs  16,856  (23.56 pct)</p>
<p> GM-Vauxhall 10,110  (12.94 pct) vs  10,950  (15.31 pct)  Peugeot	5,354   (6.85 pct) vs   4,284   (5.99 pct)</p>
<p> Volkswagen  4,269   (5.46 pct) vs   3,038   (4.25 pct)</p>
<p> Fiat	  3,959   (5.07 pct) vs   3,416   (4.77 pct)</p>
<p> Nissan	3,374   (4.32 pct) vs   4,290   (6.00 pct)</p>
<p> Renault     3,003   (3.84 pct) vs   2,022   (2.83 pct)</p>
<p> Citroen     2,298   (2.94 pct) vs   2,228   (3.11 pct)</p>
<p> BMW	   1,844   (2.36 pct) vs   1,326   (1.85 pct)</p>
<p>Top 10 marques calendar year 1996, market share in pct vs 1995.</p>
<p> Ford		   396,986 (19.6O pct) vs 410,722  (21.11 pct)</p>
<p> GM-Vauxhall	  283,989 (14.02 pct) vs 294,131  (15.12 pct)</p>
<p> Rover		  221,658 (10.94 pct) vs 240,007  (12.34 pct)</p>
<p> Peugeot		153,242  (7.57 pct) vs 143,321   (7.37 pct)</p>
<p> Renault		132,374  (6.54 pct) vs 120,485   (6.19 pct)</p>
<p> Volkswagen	   114,084  (5.63 pct) vs  81,656   (4.20 pct)</p>
<p> Nissan		  93,408  (4.61 pct) vs  91,972   (4.73 pct)</p>
<p> Fiat		    85,948  (4.24 pct) vs  70,828   (3.64 pct)</p>
<p> Citroen		 76,485  (3.78 pct) vs  80,241   (4.12 pct)</p>
<p> Toyota	60,503  (2.99 pct) vs  54,364   (2.80 pct)</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
